{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/564338-a-roman-pantheon-separate-from-the-greeks","id":564338,"title":"A Roman Pantheon separate from the Greeks.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-22T11:21:39-07:00","id":564338,"title":"A Roman Pantheon separate from the Greeks.","content":"First, the Greek Virtues wouldn't work for Rome. Piety would replace Vengence, Valour would remain in place. Intellect and Expression weren't as important to Rome as Order and Duty. So the Roman Gods would get Duty, Order, Piety, and Valour, for their virtues. Some might prefer Courage for Rome, but as brutal as Rome could be, Rome understood battle came at a cost and Peace was holy.<br /> <br /> Mars would be very different the Ares. Ares is a god of battle lust and war frenzy. Mars is the god of Adult male social roles; Farmer, Solider, Father, Priest. Mars would get Epic Stamina, and Epic Perception, Health, Fertility, War, Guardian, Justice, and Prophecy, plus the Roman PSP, would suit Mars.<br /> <br /> Venus would be more like Aphrodite, but Venus also was associated with plant fertility and with magic. So Epic Appearance, Epic Manipulation, Epic Charisma, Fertility, and Magic.<br /> <br /> I'll need to read up on the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T10:03:04-07:00","id":565502,"title":"","content":"Remember that Scion is primarily a game of MYTHOLOGY, not as much cultic practice. To differentiate the two into two pantheons, you really need to have Zeus myths that aren't Jupiter myths and Jupiter myths that aren't Zeus myths. Enough of them to make them two different guys. A superficial gloss of Mars may look really different than Ares (they really aren't as different as people think. Ares definitely did a lot of Mars-like things that don't make it into most mythology books, as they are from places that weren't Athens or from the Iliad. And Mars certainly did a crap load of Ares-like things that get swept under the carpet. For example, his parenting skills seems pretty blase and immature.), but how are the STORIES about the two different?<br /> <br /> The Romans didn't really have Virtues. Nor did the Greeks. The Greek pantheon (and related supernaturals) have Virtues. If the Roman gods are acting the same as the Greek gods (particularly since they are they same people), even if the Romans are different than the Greeks, how is that relevant? <br /> <br /> Sure there WAS a Latin (not Roman) pantheon and bits and pieces of are still around. (Those wacky gods Janus, Fevrus, Avrilus for instance. Some of whom are so obscure as to be ciphers. But they sure stuck with us...). There was also an Etruscan pantheon and the Etruscans were very intrusive into Latin life, causing a big crossover in cultic practices and some impact on mythology. (It's hard to be sure how much, because the Etruscans didn't leave anything much in the way of written myths behind. So it's cultic stuff and some cool mosaics and murals from which to figure things out.) Most of the differences in how the gods are based on how the different cultures percieve their relationship to divinity. Greeks bartered with their gods. Or bribed them. Romans drew up contracts of mutual obligations. <br /> <br /> New Scion is supposed to handle this by some &quot;mantle&quot; mechanic. So Zeus is Jupiter is Tinia (the last is quite a stretch), depending on some factor (choice? geography? who he's talking to?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T15:44:54-07:00","id":567074,"title":"","content":"Well if I understand the Roman empire, it was about putting the betterment of society before your own personal needs and desires. It conquered tribes and neighboring cultures, absorbed them into its ranks, and destroyed their sense of individuality and heritage in favor of serving the glory of Rome as a whole, rather than individuals. So I can see how Duty would be a possible Virtue for them, duty to the empire first and foremost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T19:49:26-07:00","id":636572,"title":"","content":"A friend of mine whose doctorate is in Roman and Greek comparative mythology and culture gave me a run-down on the Roman gods that flies pretty much in the face of most of what I'd ever read about them in public libraries, and most writings in Scion, too. According to her, before the Romans equated/conflated their gods with those of the Greeks, the gods the Romans followed were pure intellectual concepts, rather than anthropomorphised beings. Mars was WAR, not the god of war; Vulcanus was FIRE (and mainly destructive fire), not the god of the forge. In Scion terms, the Roman &quot;gods&quot; would be Titans. Also, before being equated with the Roman Mars concept, Ares was the god of carnage and slaughter, not anything to do with tactics, strategy, or leadership in war.<br /> <br /> In my games the Dodekatheon mainly roll their eyes at anyone who refers to Roman gods, or become insulted (or rarely, amused; they are not easily amused) if someone refers to them by their &quot;Roman name&quot;. They don't claim any especial affinity or enmity for the few surviving Etruscan gods. Ares is a psychopath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7421-celtibear","name":"CeltiBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T10:06:37-07:00","id":637140,"title":"","content":"Your friend is basing her characterization of Ares solely on Athenian Myth.<br /> <br /> Again though, none of this matters because Scion is NOT ABOUT RELIGION. It's about myth. And the Roman myths of their gods, as primarily recorded by Virgil and Ovid, are cribbed from or built directly upon the Greek myths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T10:09:49-07:00","id":637141,"title":"","content":"I mean hell - &quot;Jupiter&quot; is literally &quot;Zeu Pater&quot;, Father Zeus.<br /> <br /> There was an older Latin tradition of divinity but it was thoroughly colonized over by the Greeks (or Trojans if you believe Rome's own myths).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-25-2015, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T12:15:48-07:00","id":637253,"title":"","content":"This is really just a repeat of Ajax's point, but most of the books I've read indicate that there is little Roman mythology, either extent or even originally, i.e. they didn't really give their gods enough stories prior to importing Hellenic myths for you to really separate for something like Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T16:11:15-07:00","id":637498,"title":"","content":"I can empathize with certain members of the fan base that different incarnations of pantheons can be fairly radically different from each other depending on the exact culture, time period, and geographic period we are talking about, but we are ultimately only gonna have enough room in the books for so many pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T09:50:53-07:00","id":638118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltiBear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/564338-a-roman-pantheon-separate-from-the-greeks?p=636572#post636572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ares is a psychopath.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, of course he was. That was why the Athenians, the biggest Ares haters around, had the place where the highest, most considered and thoughtful judgement named after him. Myths about why Ares would be associated with sober justice are pretty much non-existent (not like springs and olive trees on the Acropolis, for example), but there is definitely something there that doesn't jibe with your psychopath judgement and seems to indicate there is some &quot;Mars-ness&quot; to Ares LONG before any equation with a Latin guy who was concerned with protecting the recently plowed and planted fields. (You know, the things that happen in March....). <br /> <br /> Besides the decision to use a wolf as a foster-mom (which seems like something Ares would do, not the near paladin you are turning Mars into) and then the antics of his quarrelsome and homicidal sons (more Ares-ness), what myths of Mars as exclusive to Rome? (And Virgil can't count, since he was definitely working with a pantheon that had been syncretized to Hel and back for centuries). Not that one myth like that would be enough to differentiate Ares from the different aspects that show up in Athens vs. Sparta vs. the Iliad vs. Thebes vs. etc. etc. Mars is doing Ares things a peninsula to the west of his usual stomping grounds. <br /> <br /> Once again, Scion was a game about MYTHS not cultic practice. If you don't have the myths you are facing an uphill battle that would make Sisyphus say &quot;The Hell with THAT&quot; and turn tail and run, Furies or no Furies. The typical solution has been to &quot;make it up.&quot; Which is fine. It's the only thing you really CAN do TBH, but it's difficult to try to point to anything but yourself when you do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T10:15:34-07:00","id":638141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/564338-a-roman-pantheon-separate-from-the-greeks?p=637498#post637498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can empathize with certain members of the fan base that different incarnations of pantheons can be fairly radically different from each other depending on the exact culture, time period, and geographic period we are talking about, but we are ultimately only gonna have enough room in the books for so many pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're telling me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T19:08:26-07:00","id":639703,"title":"","content":"Interesting note: Ares is the only male Olympian who doesn't have a rape myth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T21:46:37-07:00","id":639838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/564338-a-roman-pantheon-separate-from-the-greeks?p=639703#post639703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting note: Ares is the only male Olympian who doesn't have a rape myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well he does have the trial myth, where he kills the son of Posedion for raping(or nearly raping) his daughter. He is put on trial for murder, but is aquited of his crime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T22:29:09-07:00","id":639875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/564338-a-roman-pantheon-separate-from-the-greeks?p=639838#post639838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well he does have the trial myth, where he kills the son of Posedion for raping(or nearly raping) his daughter. He is put on trial for murder, but is aquited of his crime.</div> </div> </div> </div>If anything that just reinforces my point about his uniquely non-raping ways.<br /> <br /> Admittedly Ovid is vague about the conception of Romulus and Remus by Mars though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T20:47:26-07:00","id":643725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/564338-a-roman-pantheon-separate-from-the-greeks?p=639703#post639703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting note: Ares is the only male Olympian who doesn't have a rape myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, I never noticed!<br /> I wonder what it means...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T00:20:29-07:00","id":643849,"title":"","content":"Well for the Athenians (whose versions of the Greek myth we generally are speaking of because they preserved the most writing) it's mostly a matter of them not linking him in ancestry to anyone they wanted to link in ancestry to gods. But for a feminist deconstruction of the myths, it raises a lot of interesting questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}